      "hints": [
        "Differentiate $f(x) = x^2 + kx^{-1} + 2$ to find $f'(x) = 2x - \\frac{k}{x^2}$.",
        "Set $f'(2) = 0 \\implies 4 - \\frac{k}{4} = 0$ and solve for $k$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Differentiate $f(x) = x^2 + kx^{-1} + 2$ with respect to $x$:\n$$f'(x) = 2x - kx^{-2} = 2x - \\frac{k}{x^2}$$",
        "Apply the stationary point condition $f'(2) = 0$:\n$$2(2) - \\frac{k}{2^2} = 0 \\implies 4 - \\frac{k}{4} = 0$$\n$$\\frac{k}{4} = 4 \\implies k = 16$$"
      ],
